    "created_at": "2018-12-20T17:26:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-12-20T17:26:24Z",
    "body": "It is [recommended](https://lists.freedesktop.org/archives/systemd-devel/2017-January/038165.html) to use `TAG+=\"uaccess\"` in udev rules, which lets the active user session access the device. Because uaccess is processed in `73-seat-late.rules`, the file must have a number less than 73.\r\n\r\nIn my case (uDMX device) I have created `/etc/udev/rules.d/60-webusb-udmx.rules` with content:\r\n\r\n    SUBSYSTEM==\"usb\", ATTR{idVendor}==\"16c0\", ATTR{idProduct}==\"05dc\", TAG+=\"uaccess\"\r\n\r\nIt should work after unplugging and plugging back in the device (because udev rules are read whenever a device is connected).\r\nIf you have a different device and change the vid/pid, make sure the hex id number is in lowercase.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
